<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n1679" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀέλλο-πος</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ποδος</span>,
			ὁ, ἡ, for <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀελλόπους</span> (like <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀρτίπος, Οἰδίπος</span>, etc.):—<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>storm-footed, storm-swift</i>,
				<i><span class="en">
				Il.
				8.409
			</span></i>, etc. (never in <i><span class="en">
				Od.
			</span></i>); 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ἅρπυια</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Euph.
					113
				</span></i>
			; dat. pl. 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀελλοπόδεσσιν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>h.Ven.</u>
					217
				</span></i>
			: pl. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀελλόποδες, -πόδων</span>,
				<i><span class="en">
				Simon.
				7
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Pi.
				<u>N.</u>
				1.6
			</span></i>, etc.: once in Trag., <i><span class="en">
				E.
				<u>Hel.</u>
				1314
			</span></i>.—Later <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀελλοτόδης</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ου</span>, of the
			hare, <i><span class="en">
				Opp.
				<u>C.</u>
				1.413
			</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
